WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.268 line:92%
-What's up, New York? Hey.

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:05.238 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Thank you. Thank you.

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:05.839 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Hey, man.

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:09.209 size:81% position:41%
It's getting cold out.
I hate the cold, man.

00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:11.044
I hate the cold because
it bothers this metal rod

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:15.215
I got put in my left leg after
I broke it on my birthday...

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:17.650 line:92%
by going to a trampoline park.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:21.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
I went to a trampoline park
on my 24th birthday.

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:25.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
Instead of going to a
strip club like a real man.

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:27.961 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Broke my darn leg.

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:30.130 size:84% position:42%
You just gotta add that
to the list of things

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:32.332 line:92%
black people should not do.

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:36.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, we can jump.
We just don't need assistance.

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:39.072 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:42.042 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:46.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was scary
after I broke my leg

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:47.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they put me
on prescription pain meds.

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:50.450
And up until that point, I had
never done drugs in my life,

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:53.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I grew up
on the D.A.R.E. Program.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.389 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:58.691 line:92%
I'm the one kid it worked on.

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:01.094 size:75% position:38%
The D.A.R.E. Program
was effective, man,

00:01:01.094 --> 00:01:03.329 size:81% position:41%
because they made us
sing a song every day.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:06.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just a bunch of fifth graders
in class talking about...

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:07.934 line:92%
♪♪ D, I won't do drugs ♪♪

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:09.836 line:92%
♪♪ A, I'll have an attitude ♪♪

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:11.938 line:92%
♪♪ R, I will respect myself ♪♪

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:15.442 line:92%
♪♪ E, I will educate me now ♪♪

00:01:15.442 --> 00:01:18.478 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:20.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
All the teachers
looking at us like,

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:24.851
"Look at these stupid-head kids
singing this goofy song.

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:25.952 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:29.689
Y'all gotta relax and watch some
'Magic School Bus,' man."

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:31.291 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:34.027 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:41.701
Comedy. Comedy is my drug, man.
That's what I'm addicted to.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:44.104
That's why I'm glad we can all
come together and share a laugh,

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:45.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
set aside our differences
for a bit.

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:46.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think that's how to progress
in this country,

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:48.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think we'll progress
in this way.

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:49.609 size:88% position:44% line:92%
First off, black people,

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:51.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
we have to stop blaming
white people for our problems.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:53.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
All right?
It's a big deal for us.

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:58.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, white people, got to stop
creating so many problems.

00:01:58.384 --> 00:02:00.053 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:02.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know. I just --
All we're asking.

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:06.025 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
A little bit.

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:09.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've done my research
on white people. Mm-hmm.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:12.432
I be watching "Game of Thrones"
and things like that.

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:15.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
Got all types of potions
and elixirs.

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:17.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know why
shows like that exist?

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:18.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Walking Dead"
and "Game of Thrones"?

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:21.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because white people
ain't got no natural predator.

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:23.343 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:26.412
They don't.
They just got to make up stuff.

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:31.718
Sitting there like, "What if
there were zombies and dragons?

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:33.953 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Ooh!

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:35.221 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:37.624 line:92%
Oh, my word! Can you imagine?

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:39.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
What would the world be like
with problems?

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:42.862 line:92%
Oh, just save us, Khaleesi."

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:45.231 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:49.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like "Naked and Afraid"?
That's a white-ass show, bro.

00:02:49.903 --> 00:02:52.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know how good
your life got to be

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:55.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the only way
you can feel fear

00:02:55.542 --> 00:02:58.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
is go to the woods
with your ding-a-ling out?

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:00.046 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:03.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
Black people ain't doing no
"Naked and Afraid."

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:06.920 size:88% position:44%
We go outside every day,
clothed and suspected.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:09.522 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
This is no fun.

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:12.258 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:13.760 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm tellin' ya.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:17.230 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:21.000
"Will Jourdain make it past
this routine traffic stop?

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:25.104
Find out this Wednesday on
'Clothed and Suspected.'"

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:25.838 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:30.276
Set the DVR. "Clothed and
Suspected" is coming on.

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:31.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nah, I've actually
been hanging out

00:03:31.611 --> 00:03:34.047
with a lot of white people
lately because I've been

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:36.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
spending a lot of time
in Harlem.

00:03:36.149 --> 00:03:37.684 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Ahem.

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:40.119 size:84% position:42% line:92%
You guys are spreading.

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:42.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
Harlem's changed.
It's a lot different now.

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:44.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
Even the crackheads
are different.

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:46.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
Crackheads done
switched up the merchandise.

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:48.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was in the barber shop
the other day,

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:51.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
this crackhead came in and
tried to sell me a dragon egg.

00:03:51.598 --> 00:03:55.902
He's like, "Hey, man, I got
these dragon eggs for you."

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:56.970 line:92%
I was like, "Dragon egg?"

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:58.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's like, "Yeah, man,
there's a whole bag of them.

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:03.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
They nice, they clean,
they pure, they good quality.

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:05.912 line:92%
You got to buy this stuff."

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:06.479 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:10.383 size:78% position:39%
I was like, "Brother,
these are avocados."

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:12.051 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:14.621 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:21.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "How much are you
selling these for, man?"
He's like, "50 cents a piece."

00:04:21.728 --> 00:04:24.264
I was like, "Damn, that's
a great deal right there.

00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:26.799
You know how much you can get
for these on the white market?

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:29.335
You are selling yourself short,
my friend.

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:32.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's draw up a business deal.
We will take this over."

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:36.676 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:38.678
I try not to think about
that race stuff too much,

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:40.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it does seep into my mind
every now and again.

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:43.216 size:81% position:41%
I think it's because
of where I was raised.

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:44.117 line:92%
I was raised in the South.

00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:46.085
They teach things differently as
a young black kid in the South.

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:48.755
Like, I'm from a place called
Greensboro, North Carolina.

00:04:48.755 --> 00:04:50.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah. Right.

00:04:50.657 --> 00:04:52.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
And in Greensboro,
we had a planetarium.

00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:54.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I love space.
I'm infatuated with it.

00:04:54.494 --> 00:04:57.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
I love space
the way Oprah loves bread.

00:04:57.397 --> 00:04:59.198 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:00.166 size:81% position:41% line:92%
So I would get geeked.

00:05:00.166 --> 00:05:01.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would get geeked
to go to the planetarium.

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:04.170
I'd be like, "Yo, this is dope.
We're going to the planetarium.

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can't wait.
We get to learn about space."

00:05:06.172 --> 00:05:07.407 line:92%
And they say, "No, Jourdain.

00:05:07.407 --> 00:05:10.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're going to learn
about slavery."

00:05:10.176 --> 00:05:13.012 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I was like, "What? How?"

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:14.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they project stars
onto the screen,

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:16.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they say
the slaves would use the stars

00:05:16.649 --> 00:05:18.818 size:81% position:41%
as a road map of sorts
when they were trying

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:20.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
to navigate their way
to the North.

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:21.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
They'd sing songs.
They'd sing...

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:26.225
♪♪ When the first quail calls
to carry you to freedom ♪♪

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:28.795 line:92%
♪♪ Follow the drinking gourd ♪♪

00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:32.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember that song,
just in case of emergency.

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:33.499 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:36.469
So if Trump pressed that button,
I'm-a be out here...

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:39.472 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Humming ]

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:44.277 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:05:44.377 --> 00:05:46.546
"It's the North Star, Demarcus.
Follow me.

00:05:46.546 --> 00:05:48.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know a place in Harlem
where we can get

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:50.350 line:92%
some dragon eggs, my friend."

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:53.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
My name is Jourdain Fisher.
Thank you so much.

00:05:53.353 --> 00:05:54.620 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Dream on.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.556 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:56.556 --> 00:05:58.725 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, my goodness.

00:05:58.725 --> 00:06:00.660 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:03.196 line:92%
Jourdain Fisher right there!

00:06:03.196 --> 00:06:07.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not bad.
Sanding ovation. Not bad.

